{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["They said — as in the manner of: ויתל בהם אליהו ויאמר קראו בקול (1 Kings 18:27), שמח בחור בילדותיך (Ecclesiastes 11:9), באו בית אל (Amos 4:4), and many likewise. Therefore after it: ריבו באמכם ריבו (plead with your mother, plead) — how are you children of a living El when the mother has played the harlot? They are the fathers."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra appears to quote rabbinic opinion using the phrase אמרו כדרך ('they said, as is the way'), introducing examples of addresses cast in the imperative plural; the argument that 'they are the fathers' resolves the metaphor of the mother as the nation by identifying the mothers as the patriarchs."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:47.063775796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}